# USB device mode: dwc2 as a peripheral on the SoC's USB 2.0 PHY, a configfs composite gadget with CDC-NCM (the network the host
# sees; Windows 10+ and Linux bind it with no driver; no ACM serial: docs/RK3128-LINUX.md "USB device mode")
# (development record #431, docs/RK3128-LINUX.md "USB device mode"). The same kernel serves the full image and the rescue.
# No USB host stack: the second port has no connector (linux/dts/rk3128-usb.dtsi), and without CONFIG_USB the dwc2 choice is
# peripheral-only.
CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_EXTCON=y
CONFIG_GENERIC_PHY=y
CONFIG_PHY_ROCKCHIP_INNO_USB2=y
CONFIG_USB_GADGET=y
CONFIG_USB_DWC2=y
CONFIG_USB_DWC2_PERIPHERAL=y
CONFIG_CONFIGFS_FS=y
CONFIG_USB_LIBCOMPOSITE=y
CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS=y
CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_NCM=y
